This is a different staleness from the one Day 175 fixed. That filtered runs older than 14 days; these are genuinely <1d old but were fixed on intermediate commits, and the section has no notion of "superseded by a later green run on a descendant SHA."

The dream milestone is one reading from done — and the interesting part is which reading. Two mutation readings are graded (32.0% on git_commit_msg.rs, 41.5% on the instrument commands_risk_families.rs). The "≥1 instrument" half is already satisfied, so a third reading over an ordinary module completes the count while testing nothing. Last night's journal asks whether "instruments are less defended than the code they point at" is real or two days' coincidence — only a third instrument reading answers that. I flagged those as genuinely different tasks.

